## Telemetry analysis

The dashboard compares potential downtime across four Daikibo factory locations and across device types. Each unhealthy status message represents **10 minutes of potential downtime**, based on the telemetry reporting interval.

The first chart, **Downtime Per Factory**, is used as a dashboard filter. Selecting a factory shows the device-type downtime for that factory in the second chart. In the supplied dashboard image, **Daikibo Factory Seiko** has the highest factory total, and **LaserWelder** has the largest device-type total in the displayed view.

![Daikibo Telemetry Analysis dashboard](dashboard/daikibo-telemetry-dashboard.png)

### Opening the Tableau workbook

The TWB workbook points to a local source-data path from the original computer. To use it elsewhere:

1. Extract data/telemetry/daikibo-telemetry-data.json.zip into the same data/telemetry/ folder.
2. Open tableau/daikibo-telemetry-dashboard.twb in Tableau.
3. Edit the data source connection to point to data/telemetry/daikibo-telemetry-data.json, then refresh the data or extract.

## Equality-score analysis

The equality score ranges from **-100 to +100**, with **0** representing ideal equality. The completed workbook adds an Equality class column using these bands:

| Score | Class |
| --- | --- |
| -10 <= score <= 10 | Fair |
| -20 <= score < -10, or 10 < score <= 20 | Unfair |
| score < -20 or score > 20 | Highly Discriminative |

The Excel formula in row 2 is:

    =IF(ABS(C2)>20,"Highly Discriminative",IF(ABS(C2)>10,"Unfair","Fair"))

ABS(C2) measures how far the score is from zero, regardless of whether it is positive or negative. For example, -9 is **Fair**, 15 is **Unfair**, and -30 is **Highly Discriminative**.

